  "body": "## What changed\n\n- `crates/kernel/src/step_units_guard.rs` gets `UnlistedAngles`. It finds the first stated plane angle unit that is not the radian. It also finds the items that a representation with a context lists, and the pieces of those solids.\n- `crates/kernel/src/solidcore_step.rs` (`read_guarded`) uses it after the topology read:\n  - A built solid with no unit context is refused when the file states a non-radian angle unit.\n  - For an item that failed to read, the unit reason replaces the read message. The wrong angle unit is the first cause of the failure.\n- A file that states only the radian, or no angle unit, keeps such an item.\n- The refusal names the item and the angle unit, for example: `no representation gives it a unit context, so its angles would be read in radians, but the file states plane angle unit #13, which is not the radian`.\n\n## Cause\n\nThe pinned reader gives a solid item that no representation lists the default units: 1 mm per length unit and 1 radian per angle unit. Nothing checked the angle default. In a degree file, the reader read the angles of that item in radians, without a warning.\n\n## Tests\n\nPins in `crates/kernel/tests/step_short_units.rs`:\n\n- `unlisted_item_in_a_degree_file_is_refused_by_name`: the degree cone fixture with the solid #16 not listed. Red before the fix: the item was refused for an edge gap (`face #40: an edge lies 8.32 mm off the face's surface`), not for its unit.\n- `unlisted_item_that_reads_cleanly_is_refused_by_name`: the same cone with a semi-angle that reads cleanly in radians. Without the fix it imports as a wrong solid (volume 3196.7 mm^3, no warning).\n- `unlisted_item_in_a_radian_file_is_kept`: control. A millimetre and radian cube with no context imports as a 1 mm cube.\n\nMutation results:\n\n- Solid filter disabled: `unlisted_item_that_reads_cleanly_is_refused_by_name` is red (the wrong cone imports). Restored: green.\n- Failure message mapping removed: `unlisted_item_in_a_degree_file_is_refused_by_name` is red. Restored: green.\n- Radian rule removed (each angle unit counts as non-radian): `unlisted_item_in_a_radian_file_is_kept` is red. Restored: green.\n\nGate: `cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main` is green (10 steps, 0 failed). `cargo clippy -p camcraft-kernel --all-targets -- -D warnings` is clean.\n\n## Goldens moved\n\nNone.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- A file with an unlisted surface model (a sheet) in a degree file. The same filter covers it, because the reader gives sheets in `read.solids`.\n- The length unit of an item with no context. PR #2927 (issue #2919) owns that rule.\n- The heavy lanes. This change does not touch a heavy test.\n\n## Overlaps\n\n- PR #2927 touches the same function, `read_guarded` in `crates/kernel/src/solidcore_step.rs`, but different lines (it edits the solid build loop). This PR adds lines before the failure loop. PR #2927 has `needs-rework` and `conflicts`, so this PR does not stack on it. Whichever merges second refreshes.\n\nChangelog: STEP import refuses, by name, a solid item with no unit context when the file states a plane angle unit that is not the radian, so its angles are no longer read in radians without a warning.\n\nFixes #3079\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
